WEBVTT

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.238
Good news, everyone!

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:26.033
We've been hired to make
our 100th delivery.

00:00:26.118 --> 00:00:27.994
One hundred!

00:00:28.078 --> 00:00:29.537
That's almost
10 per year.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.581
This calls for a party, baby.

00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:36.002
I'm ordering 100 kegs, 100
hookers and 100 Elvis impersonators

00:00:36.086 --> 00:00:39.672
who aren't above a little
hooking, should the occasion arise.

00:00:42.926 --> 00:00:45.094
Be very gentle, folks.

00:00:45.179 --> 00:00:48.097
This is the soufflй you're
delivering to Mrs. Astor.

00:00:48.182 --> 00:00:52.018
Oh, my God, it's Elzar! Hi,
Elzar! Great soufflй, Elzar!

00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:55.271
Whatever you do,
don't drop it.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:58.441
See, Mrs. Astor takes
nitroglycerine for her heart,

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:02.320
and being a class act, she
prefers it in soufflй form.

00:01:04.698 --> 00:01:06.073
Bam!

00:01:06.158 --> 00:01:10.077
To prevent the soufflй from
exploding, Bender will carry it.

00:01:10.162 --> 00:01:12.538
He's gyroscopically stable.

00:01:31.058 --> 00:01:37.063
Look! Mrs. Astor's mansion, just
across that rickety rope bridge.

00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:42.318
Wow, it's ricketier
than it looks.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.320
You better try
to jump it, Bender.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:47.657
Okay, let me back up
for a running start.

00:01:56.291 --> 00:01:57.667
Here I go!

00:02:07.177 --> 00:02:11.097
I shall inform Mrs. Astor
that the circus is in town.

00:02:11.932 --> 00:02:13.850
Your soufflй, madam.

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:16.269
I shall take it here,
under my fork.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.080
Where's the exploding?

00:02:36.331 --> 00:02:39.834
One does not explode
in Mrs. Astor's face.

00:02:39.918 --> 00:02:42.795
I couldn't eat another bite. Hobsie?

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.427
Well done, sir.
Have you a name?

00:02:49.511 --> 00:02:52.305
Hubert Farnsworth,
at your service.

00:02:52.389 --> 00:02:55.516
A Farnsworth, you say?
Well, if I'm not mistaken,

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:58.895
the Farnsworths have been in New
New York for almost 200 years.

00:02:58.979 --> 00:03:00.646
Yes, I have.

00:03:00.731 --> 00:03:01.814
And I'm his uncle.

00:03:01.899 --> 00:03:04.483
How charmingly
unconventional.

00:03:04.568 --> 00:03:06.402
I can eat a hot dog
underwater.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:09.405
Say, would you Farnsworths
care to be my guests tomorrow

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.449
at the Astor
Endowment Fundraiser?

00:03:11.533 --> 00:03:13.409
All the best families
will be there.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.161
We can take them.

00:03:24.922 --> 00:03:29.300
On April 10, 2912,
my late husband and I

00:03:29.384 --> 00:03:32.720
set off down Fifth Avenue
aboard the Land Titanic,

00:03:32.804 --> 00:03:36.098
the largest street-going vessel ever built.

00:03:36.183 --> 00:03:40.937
Just four days into her maiden
voyage, as we approached 32nd Street,

00:03:41.021 --> 00:03:44.482
the land liner struck a mailbox and went down.

00:03:46.276 --> 00:03:51.781
2,000 souls were lost that
day, including my dear husband.

00:03:51.865 --> 00:03:55.326
In loving memory, I established
the Mr. Astor Endowment,

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:59.622
which this year supports the
United Mutant Scholarship Fund.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.793
Mutants? That's the kind of thing you are.

00:04:03.877 --> 00:04:06.212
Shh. You know mutants aren't
allowed on the surface.

00:04:06.296 --> 00:04:09.715
If anyone asks, say I'm an alien, remember?

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.634
Right. You gonna
finish that roll?

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:12.718
Shh.

00:04:12.803 --> 00:04:18.432
Now, a short film about those pitiable
creatures so in need of our charity.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:23.938
Far beneath the everyday rumble
of limousines and poodle feet,

00:04:24.022 --> 00:04:26.148
there toil
a downtrodden people

00:04:26.233 --> 00:04:29.402
even less well off
than the upper middle class.

00:04:29.486 --> 00:04:31.862
The noble sewer mutants.

00:04:31.947 --> 00:04:35.491
For, you see, generations
of exposure to toxic sewage

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:38.995
mutated them
into horrific monsters!

00:04:40.163 --> 00:04:41.205
Shut up.

00:04:41.289 --> 00:04:44.542
These industrious,
uh, people, I guess,

00:04:44.626 --> 00:04:47.336
maintain the various pipes
and poop chutes

00:04:47.421 --> 00:04:50.756
that keep decent, above-ground
society functioning.

00:04:51.466 --> 00:04:54.719
And where do these proud toileteers
learn their menial skills?

00:04:55.929 --> 00:04:57.638
At Brown University,

00:04:57.723 --> 00:05:01.559
the nation's premiere
institution of lower learning.

00:05:01.643 --> 00:05:04.020
So please, give generously,

00:05:04.104 --> 00:05:07.523
knowing some poor helpless
mutant will thank you.

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:10.109
Not in person, thank God.

00:05:12.696 --> 00:05:14.071
Well, that
was disturbing.

00:05:14.156 --> 00:05:17.241
I understand, dear.
They are hideous.

00:05:17.325 --> 00:05:20.578
Look, I guess you mean well,
but isn't that university

00:05:20.662 --> 00:05:23.664
just a tax-deductible
sewer-cleaning service?

00:05:23.749 --> 00:05:27.752
My dear, that school is about
much more than sewer pipes.

00:05:27.836 --> 00:05:28.878
Really?

00:05:28.962 --> 00:05:31.714
It's also about keeping
those filthy things busy.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:35.551
There are thousands of them
down there, breeding like rats.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.720
My great uncle
once saw a rat.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:39.138
If we don't
keep them busy,

00:05:39.222 --> 00:05:43.726
they'll start jabbering about equal
rights in their ill-bred manner.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:44.894
Let's go.

00:05:44.978 --> 00:05:47.897
If I say one more thing, I might
say it with my evening boot.

00:05:47.981 --> 00:05:50.316
Well! Rarely have I never!

00:05:50.776 --> 00:05:54.403
Please, don't blame Leela.
She's just a little ill-bred.

00:05:54.488 --> 00:05:56.405
You know how mutants are.

00:05:58.742 --> 00:06:01.410
Your companion
is a mutant?

00:06:01.495 --> 00:06:04.163
But if anyone asks,
say she's an alien.

00:06:04.247 --> 00:06:06.332
Help! Police!

00:06:08.126 --> 00:06:10.252
You may have
eluded the authorities,

00:06:10.337 --> 00:06:13.089
but don't nothing
get past Mrs. Astor.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.096
What's going to
happen to me?

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.890
Permanent deportation, you mutant.

00:06:22.974 --> 00:06:26.602
You going downtown,
baby. Way down.

00:06:35.904 --> 00:06:37.196
Incoming!

00:06:39.991 --> 00:06:40.991
Thanks, Colonel.

00:06:41.076 --> 00:06:43.369
Just doing
my job, ma'am.

00:06:50.794 --> 00:06:56.715
Mom, Dad, I can't believe I have to spend
the rest of my life in this hellhole.

00:06:57.509 --> 00:06:58.509
I'm sorry.

00:06:58.593 --> 00:07:00.177
It's okay, sweetie.

00:07:00.262 --> 00:07:04.640
Now that you're here, this hellhole
feels more like a nice, regular hole.

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:06.976
What do you say we go get some sewer coffee,

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.562
sewer cake and
Safeway ice cream.

00:07:15.277 --> 00:07:17.778
Well, the bottom's all stocked with cheap stuff.

00:07:17.863 --> 00:07:19.530
Who's in the mood
to party?

00:07:19.614 --> 00:07:21.073
Whoo!

00:07:22.284 --> 00:07:25.161
Poor Leela. I feel
like I ruined her life.

00:07:25.245 --> 00:07:26.662
You did ruin her life.

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:27.955
You might be
right, Hermes.

00:07:28.039 --> 00:07:29.039
I am right.

00:07:29.124 --> 00:07:31.625
I almost feel like we should
do something to help her.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.419
We should do something!

00:07:33.503 --> 00:07:36.130
I don't care what you say, Hermes. Let's go.

00:07:37.299 --> 00:07:40.217
Oh, mighty Mayor, we're here about Turanga Leela.

00:07:40.302 --> 00:07:41.927
You mean Leela?
Right.

00:07:42.012 --> 00:07:44.722
I mean, sure, she's a mutant,
we've known that for years,

00:07:44.806 --> 00:07:47.641
but we kept it secret 'cause
she's a fine, upstanding...

00:07:47.726 --> 00:07:50.853
Wait. You knowingly
attempted to harbor a mutant?

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.688
We did
harbor a mutant!

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:53.772
Uh-oh.

00:07:54.608 --> 00:07:57.026
Look, Leela,
there's Old Filthful.

00:08:01.406 --> 00:08:02.406
Urgh!

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.366
And there's the
West Side Pipeway.

00:08:04.451 --> 00:08:08.204
If those guys slack off for
even a second, it could explode.

00:08:08.288 --> 00:08:10.539
Hey, guys!
This is my daughter, Leela.

00:08:10.624 --> 00:08:12.166
Hey.
How you doing?

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:17.880
Well, they're with
the chuds now.

00:08:17.964 --> 00:08:20.716
These conditions
are deplorable.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:24.929
I swear, I hate every single person on the surface

00:08:25.013 --> 00:08:26.931
for making us
live like this.

00:08:29.309 --> 00:08:30.434
Leela!

00:08:30.518 --> 00:08:31.852
What are you
doing here?

00:08:31.937 --> 00:08:36.148
We were sentenced to two weeks in
the sewer for harboring a mutant.

00:08:39.319 --> 00:08:41.320
$3 at the drugstore.

00:08:41.404 --> 00:08:43.822
I'm so sorry
I ratted you out,

00:08:43.907 --> 00:08:45.783
but, you know,
after two weeks down here,

00:08:45.867 --> 00:08:48.702
I'll truly understand the
plight of the mutant people.

00:08:48.787 --> 00:08:50.079
How dare you.

00:08:50.163 --> 00:08:53.415
You want to understand
something? Look at that lake.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.584
One dip
in that toxic muck

00:08:55.669 --> 00:08:58.504
and your DNA will be
permanently mutated.

00:08:58.588 --> 00:09:01.006
You'll grow a camel hump
or a Zoidberg face.

00:09:01.091 --> 00:09:02.091
Urgh!

00:09:02.175 --> 00:09:04.218
You want to know what it's like to be a mutant?

00:09:04.302 --> 00:09:06.387
Jump in
and go for a swim.

00:09:06.471 --> 00:09:10.266
I would, but I ate a bunch of potato salad, so...

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:14.436
Yeah, that's what I thought.
You are all surface.

00:09:16.398 --> 00:09:17.398
Yeah.

00:09:20.151 --> 00:09:21.151
Hmm.

00:09:21.236 --> 00:09:24.613
Fry! Hermes!
Where my humans at?

00:09:24.698 --> 00:09:27.408
Ah, who cares? It is on.

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:31.495
Hey, hey, hey.

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:39.503
I trust the orgy pit
has been scraped and buttered?

00:09:39.587 --> 00:09:42.172
You know it. And there's mini quiches, too.

00:09:44.801 --> 00:09:48.554
It's getting cold and smelly. My
Odor-Eaters are going critical.

00:09:50.598 --> 00:09:53.058
Maybe we could plotz
in that giant cockle.

00:09:54.978 --> 00:09:57.646
Shmeepers,
it's the Land Titanic,

00:09:57.731 --> 00:10:01.025
the biggest and onlyest
land boat ever constructed.

00:10:03.778 --> 00:10:06.113
This was
one hell of a bus.

00:10:06.197 --> 00:10:10.492
Well, everyone debone a
bunk and get some shut-eye.

00:10:10.577 --> 00:10:12.578
Zoidberg,
show some respect.

00:10:12.662 --> 00:10:16.206
This is a sacred shrine to the
thousands who lost their lives.

00:10:16.291 --> 00:10:18.250
Hey, I found a safe.

00:10:20.587 --> 00:10:21.670
It's coming loose.

00:10:21.755 --> 00:10:24.923
Hand me some more
of that cruise director.

00:10:30.597 --> 00:10:32.890
The original
passenger manifest.

00:10:32.974 --> 00:10:35.809
Spreadsheets were
so elegant back then.

00:10:35.894 --> 00:10:37.811
Just one other item.

00:10:37.896 --> 00:10:42.983
It's jewelry. Jewelry!
It's jewelry, people!

00:10:43.068 --> 00:10:46.153
It's a priceless
quantum-force gemerald.

00:10:49.657 --> 00:10:51.200
What's that
enscribbled on it?

00:10:52.243 --> 00:10:54.203
"My dear Mrs. Astor.

00:10:54.287 --> 00:10:57.706
"My love for you is as
unsinkable as this land ship

00:10:57.791 --> 00:11:00.542
"and as brilliant
as this stone.

00:11:00.627 --> 00:11:02.294
"Dictated but not read,
Mr. Astor".

00:11:02.587 --> 00:11:03.670
Aw.

00:11:03.755 --> 00:11:06.131
That's so valuable.

00:11:06.216 --> 00:11:10.552
Yeah, I'll never have love
like that. Leela hates me now.

00:11:10.637 --> 00:11:12.971
Did you guys know
I have a crush on Leela?

00:11:16.101 --> 00:11:19.812
What's the matter, Leela? You've
hardly touched your toilet clams.

00:11:21.064 --> 00:11:23.232
Maybe I was too harsh
on Fry.

00:11:23.316 --> 00:11:25.275
He didn't ruin my life
on purpose.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:27.611
Things will work out,
honey. Now, here.

00:11:27.695 --> 00:11:30.697
Have some more of what looks like lemonade.

00:11:33.785 --> 00:11:37.621
We can dip left slide right
all night

00:11:37.747 --> 00:11:40.749
It's time to be wild

00:11:40.834 --> 00:11:43.127
Freestyle

00:11:44.003 --> 00:11:45.421
It's on and poppin'

00:11:45.505 --> 00:11:47.631
Ain't no stoppin'
Us from rockin'

00:11:47.715 --> 00:11:49.633
From tonight to ten o'clock

00:11:49.717 --> 00:11:53.387
Bender, I've been to wang dang
doodles all up and down the galaxy,

00:11:53.471 --> 00:11:56.515
but this is the dangest wang
I ever doodled.

00:11:56.599 --> 00:11:57.850
Oh, yeah!

00:11:58.435 --> 00:11:59.893
Come on, baby,
let's do it!

00:11:59.978 --> 00:12:01.895
Shake your booty, baby.
Come on! Yeah!

00:12:13.074 --> 00:12:15.159
This beat bangs
Here's my chance

00:12:15.243 --> 00:12:17.494
Come on, girl, let's go,
I can't...

00:12:18.705 --> 00:12:23.542
Get out! Get out! It's not fun
anymore! I want to be alone!

00:12:23.626 --> 00:12:24.710
Alone with me?

00:12:24.794 --> 00:12:26.545
I said scram, grapey!

00:12:46.816 --> 00:12:49.151
Fry? What are you doing?

00:12:49.235 --> 00:12:50.235
You were right.

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:52.571
I don't know what it's like to be a mutant.

00:12:52.655 --> 00:12:54.031
But I want to know.

00:12:54.115 --> 00:12:56.825
Wait. I never
meant for you to...

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:58.243
Oh, no!

00:13:01.498 --> 00:13:03.457
Fry! Fry!

00:13:03.917 --> 00:13:05.751
No! No!

00:13:09.506 --> 00:13:10.839
Any effect?

00:13:13.468 --> 00:13:16.220
Sorry. I tried to scream
but I barfed.

00:13:22.393 --> 00:13:25.229
I think I'm knowing what it's like to be a mutant.

00:13:25.813 --> 00:13:27.814
So what's with all
the screaming?

00:13:27.941 --> 00:13:29.399
Hey, guys.

00:13:30.902 --> 00:13:35.364
Fry, this is the stupidest,
sweetest thing you've ever done.

00:13:35.448 --> 00:13:37.574
And you know,
maybe now, together,

00:13:37.659 --> 00:13:40.285
we can be an inspiration
to other mutants.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.870
I hope so, Leela.

00:13:41.955 --> 00:13:45.082
Aw. Come here. Let me give you a kiss.

00:13:46.543 --> 00:13:47.793
Hug.

00:13:47.877 --> 00:13:49.086
Handshake.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:50.254
I'll text you.

00:13:52.465 --> 00:13:56.510
My fellow mutants, until
recently, I dwelt on the surface,

00:13:56.594 --> 00:13:59.096
where a man can gaze up at the sky in wonder

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:01.682
without a wet clump
falling in his mouth.

00:14:01.766 --> 00:14:02.766
We can do that, too.

00:14:03.977 --> 00:14:06.186
Who's ready to fight
for equality?

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:10.774
The devolution revolution
has begun!

00:14:10.858 --> 00:14:14.653
Beautiful mutants,
please welcome Devo!

00:14:17.824 --> 00:14:19.241
Hello, Sewer City.

00:14:21.244 --> 00:14:25.247
As longtime mutants ourselves, we
support your righteous struggle,

00:14:25.331 --> 00:14:27.624
and we'll do anything
we can for you!

00:14:27.709 --> 00:14:29.126
Play Whip It!
No.

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:30.460
Play the other one.

00:14:33.256 --> 00:14:35.966
It's a beautiful world
we live in

00:14:36.801 --> 00:14:39.136
A sweet romantic place

00:14:40.179 --> 00:14:42.973
Beautiful people everywhere

00:14:43.683 --> 00:14:46.351
The way they show they care

00:14:46.561 --> 00:14:48.729
Makes me want to say

00:14:49.355 --> 00:14:51.064
It's a beautiful world

00:14:51.149 --> 00:14:52.482
Ooh!

00:14:52.567 --> 00:14:54.318
It's a beautiful world

00:14:55.778 --> 00:14:57.779
It's a beautiful world

00:14:58.698 --> 00:14:59.656
For you

00:15:02.118 --> 00:15:03.410
For you

00:15:05.371 --> 00:15:06.622
For you

00:15:08.875 --> 00:15:10.334
Now that we've got
their attention,

00:15:10.418 --> 00:15:12.419
it's time to hit them
where they sit

00:15:12.503 --> 00:15:16.882
by bending the West Side Pipeway
to return all sewage to the surface.

00:15:19.636 --> 00:15:23.305
But who could possibly bend such a huge pipe?

00:15:24.515 --> 00:15:27.976
So lonely.
Poor, sad Bender.

00:15:28.394 --> 00:15:30.062
Hey, buddy.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.898
What the heck?

00:15:34.525 --> 00:15:38.487
Bend it! Bend it! Bend it!

00:15:47.997 --> 00:15:50.582
What goes down must back up.

00:16:00.259 --> 00:16:04.638
Yucks. I picked the wrong day
to wear my new Crocses.

00:16:04.722 --> 00:16:08.809
Prepare to storm the surface
for the Million Mutant March!

00:16:11.312 --> 00:16:12.604
Move out, Fry.

00:16:12.689 --> 00:16:15.524
We need our most disgusting
mutant leading the charge.

00:16:15.608 --> 00:16:18.360
I'll meet you up there. I need
to check out something first.

00:16:18.444 --> 00:16:20.570
Okay. Vyolet,
you're up front.

00:16:20.655 --> 00:16:21.655
Hey!

00:16:23.282 --> 00:16:26.702
Mayor, this sewer debacle
has gone on long enough.

00:16:26.786 --> 00:16:31.331
As your largest campaign
contributor, I demand action!

00:16:31.416 --> 00:16:34.292
Very well.
$80 worth of action it is.

00:16:35.545 --> 00:16:36.545
Voilа.

00:16:36.629 --> 00:16:41.049
We simply pump the fruits of our
excretion into Madison Cube Garden.

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:44.970
Well, it seems
everything is under...

00:16:50.393 --> 00:16:51.518
Two!
Four!

00:16:51.602 --> 00:16:52.728
Six eyes!

00:16:52.812 --> 00:16:55.313
The mutant people
will arise!

00:16:55.398 --> 00:16:58.567
The segregation of the mutant people ends today.

00:16:58.651 --> 00:17:02.904
We demand equal rights,
equal access to the surface,

00:17:02.989 --> 00:17:05.699
and the blood of
your first-born children.

00:17:05.825 --> 00:17:08.910
That's so we have something
to give up in the negotiations.

00:17:08.995 --> 00:17:13.165
I've never been so moved, and
I see no reason to begin now.

00:17:13.249 --> 00:17:17.544
Hobsie, flush those creatures back
down the hole they crawled out of.

00:17:17.628 --> 00:17:19.713
Madam's sewage-seeking
missile.

00:17:40.026 --> 00:17:42.235
Let my people stay!

00:17:49.702 --> 00:17:50.827
Neat.

00:17:51.454 --> 00:17:53.288
Mrs. Astor,
deep in the sewer,

00:17:53.372 --> 00:17:55.749
we discovered the wreck
of the Land Titanic,

00:17:55.833 --> 00:17:57.626
on which your husband
land-drowned.

00:17:57.710 --> 00:18:00.837
Inside was something
that might interest you.

00:18:00.922 --> 00:18:05.342
The gemerald ring my husband was
to give me in lieu of children.

00:18:05.426 --> 00:18:08.428
So what? I have a chandelier
in my car made of those.

00:18:08.513 --> 00:18:11.139
Not the gem.
This passenger manifest.

00:18:11.224 --> 00:18:13.266
It turns out there were mutants on that ship

00:18:13.351 --> 00:18:15.435
working below deck
in the sewage galley.

00:18:16.062 --> 00:18:17.103
Ma'am?

00:18:17.188 --> 00:18:20.106
I was just a young girl.

00:18:20.191 --> 00:18:22.651
Drain angels,
they called us.

00:18:22.735 --> 00:18:25.070
When the ship
started going down,

00:18:25.154 --> 00:18:29.115
my mother grabbed me and
made for the nearest life-car.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:35.580
But the places were all taken
by surface passengers.

00:18:35.665 --> 00:18:38.291
As my mother held me tight,

00:18:38.376 --> 00:18:42.879
I suddenly felt the gentle
tap of a cane on my face.

00:18:42.964 --> 00:18:47.717
I turned to see the kindly smile of Mr. Astor.

00:18:59.564 --> 00:19:02.274
Thanks to your
husband's humanity,

00:19:02.358 --> 00:19:07.612
I lived to raise my own daughter,
and she, a daughter in turn.

00:19:07.697 --> 00:19:10.448
Mom, why have I
never heard this?

00:19:10.533 --> 00:19:12.242
My mother's nuts.

00:19:12.326 --> 00:19:13.952
I beg you,
Mrs. Astor,

00:19:14.036 --> 00:19:16.705
if you truly want to honor your husband's memory,

00:19:16.789 --> 00:19:20.250
treat these people
with dignity, as he did.

00:19:20.334 --> 00:19:23.795
Oh, he was
a dear man, Mr. Astor.

00:19:24.463 --> 00:19:27.549
Randall, let's grant
these mutants their freedom.

00:19:27.633 --> 00:19:28.675
Okay.

00:19:30.511 --> 00:19:32.262
Are we not men now?

00:19:32.346 --> 00:19:35.098
I'm 40% potato,
but close enough.

00:19:35.182 --> 00:19:36.766
Thank you, Fry.

00:19:36.851 --> 00:19:39.644
I think maybe I can
stomach that kiss now.

00:19:44.817 --> 00:19:46.067
What the...

00:19:46.152 --> 00:19:48.194
Good afternoon.
I am Mr. Astor.

00:19:48.279 --> 00:19:50.363
I did not perish
that fateful day,

00:19:50.448 --> 00:19:52.824
but rather plummeted
into the toxic lake,

00:19:52.909 --> 00:19:55.076
where I mutated
and lived in solitude

00:19:55.161 --> 00:19:59.164
until this ruddy lad here stepped
into my mouth and lodged there.

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:02.292
Mister?
Is that really you?

00:20:04.337 --> 00:20:08.506
Hooray! A happy ending
for the rich people!

00:20:12.303 --> 00:20:16.306
Mom, Dad, Grandma,
this is where I work.

00:20:16.432 --> 00:20:17.641
Oh!

00:20:18.434 --> 00:20:19.851
Was there a fire?

00:20:19.936 --> 00:20:21.895
So, Bender,
how was the party?

00:20:21.979 --> 00:20:24.230
Only the greatest
party ever!

00:20:24.315 --> 00:20:26.691
I don't need to have another
party in my whole life.

00:20:26.776 --> 00:20:28.568
I am partied out!

00:20:28.653 --> 00:20:30.528
Dang.
Sorry we missed it.

00:20:31.113 --> 00:20:35.283
We could have another one, if it
would make you guys feel better.

00:20:35.368 --> 00:20:37.452
Really? No,
that's not necessary.

00:20:37.536 --> 00:20:38.954
Hit it, Bender!

00:20:39.163 --> 00:20:41.498
Bend it, bend it

00:20:41.582 --> 00:20:43.500
Just a little bit

00:20:43.584 --> 00:20:45.752
And take it easy

00:20:45.878 --> 00:20:47.629
Show you're likin' it

00:20:47.713 --> 00:20:51.466
And, lover, you know
that we're gonna hit

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.719
The heights 'cause I'm sure that we're made to fit

00:20:54.804 --> 00:20:57.764
Together, just like
pieces of a

00:20:57.867 --> 00:20:59.994
Jigsaw puzzle

00:21:00.059 --> 00:21:02.686
What's the hustle?